; form-native-decode-encoding-band.fk — the FOUR-WAY-PROVABLE half of form-native-decode.fk:
; the synthetic-input formula and the comparison primitive fnd-run reads its verdict through,
; neither of which touches Metal.
;
; WHY THIS IS SEPARATE FROM form-native-decode-band.fk. That file's fnd-run calls
; metal_buf_from_file / metal_pipeline / metal_enqueue / metal_sync / metal_buf_read — a real GPU
; is a host organ, not a fourth walker, so no manifest entry can honestly claim four-way agreement
; over it (the same reason metal-door-band.fk and metal-handle-door-band.fk are witnesses, not
; manifest rows). But form-native-decode.fk ALSO defines pure Form arithmetic that has nothing to
; do with Metal — fnd-x-val/fnd-x-list (the synthetic vector) and fnd-maxdiff (the comparison the
; GPU witness reads its verdict through). THAT arithmetic is exactly as four-way-provable as any
; other Form recipe, and burying it inside a Metal-gated file would have hidden a claim this
; repo's own discipline says to register: "register in fourth-arm-bands.txt only the genuinely
; four-way-provable claims (the encoding math)."
;
; ONE CHECK NAMED OUT, NOT SILENTLY DROPPED: fnd-x-bytes (the IEEE-754 byte string md-le32/
; md-f32-bits build for the GPU binding) is NOT tested here. Measured directly (Go/Rust/TS fed
; the same canonical multi-file source list validate.sh's own fk_expand_declared_deps resolves):
; a 12-float, 48-byte string built by byte_to_str + str_concat comes back str_len 54 on ALL THREE
; walkers, and the decoded values are wrong (e.g. element 0 read back as -1.78e-38 instead of the
; encoded 1.0) — every byte >= 0x80 is being read or re-encoded as UTF-8 rather than held as a raw
; octet, inflating a 48-byte binary string to 54 bytes before anything downstream sees it. This is
; a WIDER version of equireach.fk's own documented gap (that header only names it for
; `read_file_slice`-sourced bytes on rust/ts; this is byte_to_str/str_concat-CONSTRUCTED bytes,
; and it reproduces on Go too) — not a bug this band introduces, a real limit of holding arbitrary
; binary octets in a Form string on three of the four walkers. form-native-decode-band.fk's GPU
; witness still exercises fnd-x-bytes for real (it has to — that is what crosses the door), and it
; is CORRECT there: fkwu's own string representation is byte-faithful (the discipline
; kat-token-handle.fk / llama-token-handle.fk already lean on), and the GPU round trip measured
; max|Δ| = 0. What is refused here is claiming that correctness FOUR-WAY when three of the four
; arms cannot even hold the bytes without corrupting them.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/format-arith.fk form-stdlib/metal-door.fk form-stdlib/equireach.fk form-stdlib/equireach-gguf.fk form-stdlib/gguf-meta.fk native/metal/whole-tensor-residency.fk form-stdlib/llama-decode-msl.fk form-stdlib/llama-numerics.fk form-stdlib/form-native-decode.fk
;
; Proven by: this file. Verdict 3 reproduced identically on fkwu (repo-root fkwu-uni.c, --src
; door, self-resolving preludes) and, fed the SAME canonical source list validate.sh's own
; fk_expand_declared_deps computes, on form-kernel-go/bin-go, form-kernel-rust and form-kernel-ts
; directly (all three agree with each other and with fkwu). NOT YET REGISTERED in
; fourth-arm-bands.txt: this checkout's validate.sh currently refuses to run ANY band —
; `validate_fkwu_native_surface: FAIL (11 error(s))`, reproduced identically against an
; already-merged, unrelated band (form-stdlib/tests/moe-gate-band.fk) on a clean fetch of origin/
; main, so it is a pre-existing repo-wide gate (the metal_* op family is not wired into the fkc
; flattener's explicit-arity tables) and not something this task's slice caused or can honestly
; fix inside its own scope. Registering a manifest row requires that gate healthy first.

(do
    ; ---- bit 1: the synthetic input is the closed form the header states — hand-checkable:
    ; x_0=1, x_1=2 ... x_10=11, x_11=1 (wraps at the mod-11 boundary) ----
    (let xs (fnd-x-list 12))
    (let x-ok (if (str_eq (int_to_str (float_to_int (nth xs 0))) "1")
                (if (str_eq (int_to_str (float_to_int (nth xs 10))) "11")
                    (if (str_eq (int_to_str (float_to_int (nth xs 11))) "1") 1 0) 0) 0))

    ; ---- bit 2: fnd-maxdiff itself — zero on identical lists, exactly the stated delta on lists
    ; that differ by a known amount. This is the same comparison fnd-run's `maxdiff` is built from. ----
    (let same-ok (if (eq (fnd-maxdiff (list 1.0 2.0 3.0) (list 1.0 2.0 3.0)) 0.0) 1 0))
    (let diff-ok (if (eq (fnd-maxdiff (list 1.0 2.0 3.0) (list 1.0 2.0 3.5)) 0.5) 1 0))
    (let maxdiff-ok (if (eq same-ok 1) (if (eq diff-ok 1) 1 0) 0))

    (add (mul x-ok 1) (mul maxdiff-ok 2)))
